  "id": "Compound::DB00642 - Disease::DOID:1324",
  "verbalization": "Pemetrexed, a folic acid metabolism inhibitor, is linked to Lung Cancer through its inclusion in the Folic Acid Metabolism Inhibitors pathway, which includes Methotrexate. Methotrexate is known to treat Lung Cancer, suggesting a potential therapeutic relationship between Pemetrexed and the disease. The shared lowest common ancestor, Carboxylic Acid and Enzyme Inhibitor, highlights a common biochemical mechanism that may underlie the observed effects. The evidence suggests that Pemetrexed may contribute to Lung Cancer through a pathway involving folic acid metabolism and enzyme inhibition, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Methotrexate and the role of enzyme inhibition provide a framework for understanding the potential impact of Pemetrexed on Lung Cancer.",
